/*! \mainpage Ion Beam Simulation Package

IBSimu is a simulation package for ion beam optics capable of solving
electric fields in 1D, 2D (planar or cylindrical symmetry) or full 3D
simulation geometries. The code features a non-relativistic particle
ray tracing with space charge deposition to a mesh for reaching
self-consistent solutions of high space charge particle beams using
Vlasov iteration. The code also features a model for positive ion
plasma extraction.

The code is used via C++ programming language for, which enables
powerful use of automation and makes the code versatile. The code is
still easy to use because of logical division of features into modules
(C++ classes).  The code also features an interactive easy-to-use
post-processing tool for diagnosing fields and particle trajectories.

The code's manual consists of the reference manual and an 
\subpage p_intro "introduction", which describes the different concepts
in the simulations in couple of pages.  The reference manual describes the
classes, functions and variables of the IBSimu package in detail, but
first time users should first read the introduction to get a grasp of
the parts of the package and how they use each other.
 
*/





/*! \page p_intro Introduction

